GAL22V10
BUSDBG

AS   DS   RW   FC0  FC1  FC2  A19  RESET PHI2G WBUF LE   GND
BERR PHI1 BPHI2 BRW RAMRW TRIG BERRL DBG0 DBG1 DBG2 DBG3 VCC

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; MC68008 core board, GAL3: Junior bus clocks and strobes, plus debug aids.
; Replaces the 74HCT14 and 74LS01 of earlier drafts. All combinational.
;
; Bus side (fixed, do not change):
;   PHI1, BPHI2  bus clocks made from GAL2's PHI2 (PHI2G); both come out of
;                this one chip, so they are aligned to within a few ns.
;   BRW          bus R/W: low only during a window write (WBUF low).
;   RAMRW        Junior RAM.RW write strobe: low while LE (= PHI2 high in a
;                window cycle) and writing. Driven push-pull.
;
; Debug side (edit freely, reprogram, no board change needed):
;   TRIG   logic-analyser trigger, active low. Default: interrupt acknowledge.
;   BERRL  sticky bus-error flag, active low, drives the red BERR LED.
;          Set by any BERR, cleared by reset (RESET = ~PORST).
;   DBG0-3 spare probes on the logic-analyser header / test point.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

PHI1    = /PHI2G
BPHI2   = PHI2G
BRW     = WBUF
/RAMRW  = LE * /WBUF

/TRIG   = /AS * FC2 * FC1 * FC0

/BERRL  = /BERR
        + /BERRL * RESET

/DBG0   = /AS * /RW                    ; any write cycle
/DBG1   = /AS * FC2 * FC1 * /FC0       ; supervisor program fetch
/DBG2   = /AS * A19                    ; access to the upper half (ROM, window, I/O)
/DBG3   = /AS * /FC2                   ; user-mode cycle

DESCRIPTION
68008 core board GAL3: Junior bus PHI1/PHI2/R/W/RAM.RW, logic-analyser
trigger, sticky BERR flag and spare debug outputs.
